Package: oosccohort
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Cohort Model for Out-of-School Rates
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Ziyi", "Zhou", email = "204588615+EllenSyuu@users.noreply.github.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An independent implementation, written from the published
    methodology, of the Bayesian cohort model for out-of-school rates
    (SDG indicator 4.1.4) described by Dharamshi, Barakat, Antoninis and
    Montoya (2022). Administrative rates are modelled in real space and
    survey rates in probit space; a smoothed random walk with drift gives the
    entry-age baseline and a two-dimensional P-spline surface gives the
    changes along each school-entry cohort. The package validates input data
    against a documented contract, builds the model input, fits the model
    with 'rstan' and reports age-specific rates with credible intervals. It
    is not an official UNESCO product and does not produce official
    estimates.
